80% of the data is used for training the machine learning model, while the remaining 20% is used for testing its performance on unseen data.


TASK 3

Given a simple linear regression model predicting song popularity from danceability, intentionally use only 5% of the data for training and 95% for testing. Observe the model's performance and explain whether this is likely to cause underfitting or overfitting.

CODE:

import pandas as pd
from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split
from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression
from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error, r2_score

df = pd.read_csv("spotify.csv")

# Use Danceability as the only feature
X = df[["Danceability"]]
y = df["Popularity"]

# Use only 5% for training and 95% for testing
X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(
    X, y, test_size=0.95, random_state=42
)

# Create and train the model
model = LinearRegression()
model.fit(X_train, y_train)

# Predictions
train_pred = model.predict(X_train)
test_pred = model.predict(X_test)

# Calculate errors
train_error = mean_squared_error(y_train, train_pred)
test_error = mean_squared_error(y_test, test_pred)

print("Training rows:", len(X_train))
print("Testing rows:", len(X_test))
print("Training MSE:", train_error)
print("Testing MSE:", test_error)

print("Training R2 Score:", r2_score(y_train, train_pred))
print("Testing R2 Score:", r2_score(y_test, test_pred))


ANSWER:

Using only 5% of the dataset for training gives the model very little data to learn from. Since the model has insufficient training examples, it is likely to have poor predictive performance. This situation is more likely to cause UNDERFITTING rather than overfitting.

Underfitting happens when a model cannot learn the underlying relationship in the data properly. In this case, using only 5% of the data makes it difficult for the model to learn a reliable relationship between danceability and popularity.

The training and testing errors can be compared to support this conclusion. A model that performs poorly because it has not learned enough from the data is showing signs of underfitting.


